From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:11:41 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Memory pressure on Windows 10 Mobile: told when it ends,
 re-armed while serious, and the address space watched

Nothing ever told the engine that memory pressure was over, so after the
first low-memory of a run every later one came out as low-memory-ongoing,
and nsJSEnvironment does not collect on that. A Lumia 650 sat over its
390 MB limit for minutes, told ongoing again and again without another
shrinking GC, until the system ended the app.

gecko_w10m_memory_pressure moves from HeadlessCompositorWidget.cpp to
widget/headless/GeckoW10mMemoryPressure.cpp, which decides on the main
thread what the engine is told:
- pressure comes on with a fresh low-memory (the collection runs inside the
  notification; the note says how long it took) and ends with
  memory-pressure-stop when the shell says Low again;
- while it is serious (the phone at High or over its limit, the address
  space low, or a JS allocation that failed) it is told afresh every
  memory.gecko-w10m.pressure-rearm-ms (30 s): stop, then a new low-memory.
  Medium, where a 1 GB Lumia spends much of a session, gets one fresh
  collection and the cheap ongoing after that;
- pressure that comes back within 10 s of the last collection waits out the
  rest, so the inputs flipping cannot start GC after GC.

A watcher on a background task queue walks the address space with
VirtualQuery every 5 s, every second when the largest free piece is within
twice memory.gecko-w10m.address-space.low-mb (96). Below that the engine is
put under pressure until the piece is back above one and a half times it.
On the HP Elite x3 Discord left 300-400 MB free with nothing over 17 MB in
one piece, with the phone nowhere near its limit. Notes: 'vm watch: ...'
and 'mem: pressure on / still under pressure / pressure over'.

The first JS allocation failure of a run (js/src/vm/Runtime.cpp) asks for a
fresh low-memory as well, after the address-space map. Started from
XRE_mainRun just before the main loop; before that the shell's word goes in
as it always did.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 js/src/vm/Runtime.cpp                        |  10 +-
 modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml     |  27 +
 toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp                  |   8 +
 widget/headless/GeckoW10mMemoryPressure.cpp  | 651 +++++++++++++++++++
 widget/headless/HeadlessCompositorWidget.cpp |  12 +-
 widget/headless/moz.build                    |   8 +
 6 files changed, 706 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 widget/headless/GeckoW10mMemoryPressure.cpp

diff --git a/js/src/vm/Runtime.cpp b/js/src/vm/Runtime.cpp
index 862301133b..1b26e987a0 100644
--- a/js/src/vm/Runtime.cpp
+++ b/js/src/vm/Runtime.cpp
@@ -684,6 +684,7 @@ js::HashNumber JSRuntime::randomHashCode() {
 #  include "mozilla/Sprintf.h"
 #  include "util/WindowsWrapper.h"
 extern "C" void GeckoW10mNoteAddressSpaceOnFailure(const char* aWhy);
+extern "C" void GeckoW10mMemoryPressureOnFailure(const char* aWhy);
 extern "C" void GeckoW10mNote(const char* text);
 extern "C" IMAGE_DOS_HEADER __ImageBase;
 
@@ -730,9 +731,16 @@ static void GeckoW10mNoteMallocFailure(JSRuntime* aRuntime,
                  unsigned((uintptr_t(aCaller) & ~uintptr_t(1)) -
                           uintptr_t(&__ImageBase)));
   GeckoW10mNote(note);
-  // The first one: what the address space was made of when it happened.
+  // The first one: what the address space was made of when it happened. And
+  // then the engine is asked to let go -- a fresh "low-memory", a shrinking
+  // GC and a cycle collection -- which nothing asked for before: a run that
+  // had been told about memory once already only ever heard "ongoing" again,
+  // and the JS engine ignores that
+  // (widget/headless/GeckoW10mMemoryPressure.cpp). After the map, so that
+  // the map is of the moment it failed.
   if (drawn == 0) {
     GeckoW10mNoteAddressSpaceOnFailure("a JS allocation failed");
+    GeckoW10mMemoryPressureOnFailure("a JS allocation failed");
   }
 
   // The direct caller is a vector's allocation policy, which says nothing.
diff --git a/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml b/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
index 38d7296208..e3c6bfb05b 100644
--- a/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
+++ b/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
@@ -14365,6 +14365,33 @@
   value: 180000
   mirror: always
 
+#if defined(GECKO_W10M)
+# The process's own address space, watched from a background task queue
+# (widget/headless/GeckoW10mMemoryPressure.cpp): a 32-bit process has 2 GB of
+# it, and on the phones it runs out in pieces before memory runs out -- the
+# HP Elite x3 had 300-400 MB free and nothing over 17 MB in one piece. When
+# the largest free piece falls below this many MB the engine is put under
+# memory pressure (a shrinking GC, a cycle collection, the caches) until the
+# piece is back above one and a half times this. Walked every 5 s, every
+# second within twice this. 0 turns the watcher off.
+- name: memory.gecko-w10m.address-space.low-mb
+  type: RelaxedAtomicUint32
+  value: 96
+  mirror: always
+
+# While the engine is under serious memory pressure -- the phone at High or
+# over its limit, the address space low, an allocation that failed -- it is
+# told again this often: memory-pressure-stop and then a fresh low-memory,
+# which runs another shrinking GC and cycle collection, instead of
+# low-memory-ongoing, which the JS engine ignores. Medium gets one fresh
+# low-memory when it comes on and the cheap ongoing after that. 0 tells it
+# once per spell of pressure, as upstream does.
+- name: memory.gecko-w10m.pressure-rearm-ms
+  type: RelaxedAtomicUint32
+  value: 30000
+  mirror: always
+#endif
+
 #---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 # Prefs starting with "middlemouse."
 #---------------------------------------------------------------------------
